{#- GoatCounter, as a beacon rather than a script.

   No cookies, nothing stored on the reader's machine, no personal data and so
   no consent banner to put in front of the writing. That is the whole reason
   it is GoatCounter and not something that follows people around.

   THE PIXEL, NOT count.js
   -----------------------
   GoatCounter's documented default is a <script> from gc.zgo.at. Measured on
   2026-08-30 that file is 9,213 bytes raw and 3,358 gzipped — more than this
   site's entire stylesheet costs (3,059), and more than half of what all four
   of its own scripts cost together. On a site whose colophon prints its own
   page weight, and whose largest outstanding saving is 3.6 kB of comments in
   the JS, spending 3.4 kB a page on counting the page is the wrong trade.

   The beacon is the same endpoint without the script: the request the script
   would have made, made by the document instead. It costs the tag below and a
   1x1 GIF in reply, so it does not move the Weight row at all — where count.js
   would have put every post up by 3 kB and would not even have been counted,
   since subresources() in page-weight.js only matches root-relative src.

   What it gives up, and it is worth knowing before switching back:

     - no screen size, and no way to tell whether JS ran
     - more crawler noise. GoatCounter filters known bots server-side by user
       agent, but an image prefetcher looks more like a reader than a script
       that never ran does.

   Both are page views, referrers and unique-ish visitors, which is what was
   asked for. To go back to the script, this file is the only thing to change
   — and page-weight.js would then need to account for it, or the colophon
   starts under-reporting by 3 kB.

   Off until site.goatcounter is set: the account has to exist first, and a
   beacon pointing at a site code that does not resolve is a 404 on every page
   load. -#}
{%- if site.goatcounter %}
{%- set beaconTitle = title if title else "Ralph Hawkins" %}
<img src="https://{{ site.goatcounter }}.goatcounter.com/count?p={{ page.url | urlencode }}&amp;t={{ beaconTitle | urlencode }}"
     alt="" width="1" height="1" style="position:absolute;pointer-events:none">
{%- endif %}
